You've had the leaderboard tab open for days, scrolled past the same thumbnails, and clicked into nothing. Happens to all of us. Here's what's actually new this week.

@omare turned a personal list into Inspirational Women — a gallery of women whose discipline, courage and mindset changed how he thinks and decides to spend his days. It's less a website, more a thank-you note you scroll through. @teni built Stay In Touch on a painfully honest premise: "I'll text them later" never works. It helps you set a rhythm of calls and visits with the people who matter, plus shared history so nothing slips. And @maadandev's NextRole NG takes a swing at CV tools that hand out fake 90% scores — it tells you the truth about how Nigerian recruiters read your CV and shows exactly what to fix.

One small ask: go to l2e.lovable.app and vote for the build that hit hardest. Leaderboard resets Friday.
